// The release-tag ruleset: a pushed `v*` tag cannot be moved or deleted.
//
// A record, as `default-branch.json` beside it is. GitHub does not read this
// path. What enforces the property is the ruleset this file was POSTed as, and
// `GET /repos/Eaiger-Ent/ee-standard/rulesets` is how to see that it still does.
//
// **Why it exists.** An adopter pins the checker as
// `register-check @ git+https://github.com/Eaiger-Ent/ee-standard@v0.9.0`
// (ADR 0032), and ADR 0032 justified that pin by calling the tag immutable. A
// git tag is not immutable. Until 2026-10-24 this repository had no tag ruleset
// and immutable releases were off, so anyone with write access could have
// moved `v0.9.0` to another commit. An adopter's `uv.lock` records the commit
// it resolved, so a frozen install was safe. The next re-lock would have taken
// whatever the tag then named, with nothing in the diff but a hash.
//
// GitHub's immutable releases, enabled the same day, lock a release's tag once
// the release is published. They apply only to releases published after they
// were enabled, and not to a tag before its release exists. This ruleset covers
// both: every existing `v*` tag, and each new one from the moment it is pushed.
//
// **No bypass, on purpose.** The release procedure pushes the tag before its
// pull request is reviewed. If review then changes the commit, the tag cannot
// follow it, and the release is cut as the next patch version instead. A
// version that was pushed may have been fetched, so it is not reused.
//
// Not a control, and deliberately not in `controls.yaml`. Tag immutability is
// a property of this repository as the publisher of the checker, not of a
// conformant Equal Experts repository, most of which publish nothing pinned by
// tag. `tests/test_release_tags.py` holds this file's shape. It cannot see the
// platform, which is what `default-branch.json`'s header says too.
{
  "name": "release-tags",
  "target": "tag",
  "enforcement": "active",
  "conditions": {
    "ref_name": {
      "include": ["refs/tags/v*"],
      "exclude": []
    }
  },
  "rules": [
    { "type": "update" },
    { "type": "deletion" }
  ],
  "bypass_actors": []
}
